 we'll be  focusing on in this presentation  both of these different programs are  aimed towards treating multiple myeloma  and similar to bb 2121 2121-7  is an anti-bcma car t therapy and it's  currently under clinical investigation  for the treatment  of relapsed or refractory multiple  myeloma  as is shown here it's currently in phase  two  we currently have many different  programs that are in various stages  but those are those are getting  earlier stage than the bb 2121  and 2121.7  i should iterate that all of these  products are investigational  so right now we're investigating the  safety and efficacy but it has not yet  been established  so none of these project products have  yet been approved for use by any health  authority  but our whole sincere hope is that they  are soon  so let's get into now how the car t  cells are manufactured  it all starts with a leukopheresis  the patient's blood is drawn and the  peripheral blood  um is then isolated uh  by a like a fico gradient separation  we isolate the pbmc using this method  and the pbmc are our starting material  that we would begin our cartoon  manufacturing process with  the cells are then transduced with the  lentiviral vector  and then the t cells are expanded with a  selective  expansion cocktail and then this is  grown in a bioreactor for about seven to  ten days  at this point the car t  drug product is now made so this is a  final product that's grown and these car  t drug products  are able to be infused into a patient  so it goes all the way from the patient  being drawn with their own cells  to the medicine that is uh then  formulated at the end of this process  so bp 21 21 and 21 21  7 as i had mentioned are directed  towards bcma  this is for the treatment of multiple  myeloma  for a little bit of background multiple  myeloma is a cancer  of plasma cells and it's often  characterized by  hyper proliferation of the malignant  plasma cells in the bone marrow  this can result in renal failure 