nction longer  than ones that aren't enriched for it  and they may function longer in models  of  of potential relapse or refractory  disease as  is often seen in multiple myeloma  and this persistence of the functional  car t cells after infusion  may be a determinant actually of the  duration of the response which is going  to really be key  as we evaluate this model  we had some early evidence that supports  that this particular compound  may could confer a more durable  anti-tumor response  so this was an in vivo study that was  done at bluebird  in-house with uh some of our our animal  studies that were done  so what this is a tumor model a  xenograft model  where a tumor was implanted into a mouse  a primary tumor  and then car ts were car t cells were  administered anti-vcma car t cells  what we can see here is that in this  primary challenge  both a standard car t cell and one that  is supplemented with this compound  controlled the tumor but then a  re-challenge of the tumor  was was then administered  and at this tumor re-challenge there was  no tumor growth in mice that were  treated with uh this particular  bb 21 21 7 process so with the pi3  kinase inhibitor  but the ones that did not have this pi3  kinase inhibitor  actually develop disease or outgrowth of  the tumor  after after it was administered so this  suggests  longer persistence of the anti-tumor  effect of the car t  due to the presence of this particular  compound  so now we're going to get into why uh  why are we using cyto for this project  and it really comes down to one major  question  we want to understand what  characteristics of the car t cells  within the drug  product so that final formulated  material that's being infused into the  patient  and how those correlate with patient  response  we're going about that using um  using a particular panel that we  developed in-house to sort of deepen our  understanding  of what this drug product is  to do this we used a 37 marker panel  that 